CoralFlower 0.7.1 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/FicusFicusov/CoralFlower tag v0.7.1
(commit 46790b943bdb5e4143212d83dc495c832eefdbb8; source: https://github.com/FicusFicusov/CoralFlower/archive/46790b943bdb5e4143212d83dc495c832eefdbb8.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. CoralFlower by FicusFicusov (CoralFlower contributors), a fork of ChoralRoot FM-1 (Quixotic7, ChoralRoot FM-1 contributors), a fork of Felucca:
Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments (Felucca); the FM6 engine Melodee's, Copyright (C) 2026 Kerem Kilic (Ellic Studio).
Ported parts keep their licences (msfa in fm6_core.c: Apache-2.0, Dexed: GPL-3.0-or-later; the UI faces Inter Tight and Departure Mono and the Fukiai icons are rasterised in: OFL 1.1, MIT):
CoralFlower's LICENSING.md, LICENSING-choralroot.md (its docs/LICENSING-choralroot.md) and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file. The JieLi SDK files of CoralFlower's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/coralflower_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as CoralFlower's own browser emulator and host tests do (tools/emu/web/emu_web.c,
tools/emu/emu_fw.c, tools/emu/emu_firmware.h, tests/cf_backup_test.c) and adds the USB SysEx path (usb.c, cf_backup.c's backup protocol, ota.c's identity handshake); the hardware stand-ins are the emulator's:
keys/LEDs/LCD, the MASTER pot, NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, one core (the bass part's job runs inline), USB = always configured (SysEx and MIDI out through usb.c's rings),
no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no serial console, no updater and no USB boot (ota.c answers the identity handshake only).
Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h; tools/emu/web/compat from CoralFlower's tree).

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/FicusFicusov/CoralFlower at commit 46790b943bdb5e4143212d83dc495c832eefdbb8
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py, the glue tools/studio/coralflower_studio.c and the shim tools/wasm_shim. A tarball of exactly this commit
